this year's sakharov prize for freedom  of thought will be awarded to the  imprisoned russian opposition figure  alexey navalny for his fight for  democracy in russia his daughter daria  will receive the award on his behalf  parliament will adopt its position on  the new digital markets act it's set to  call for stricter regulation of the  so-called gatekeepers of the internet to  better protect consumers and their data  the rules would apply to powerful giants  like search engines social networks and  advertisers  ahead of the eu leaders summit later  this month meps will debate the pandemic  situation they're also expected to voice  concerns about how global supply chains  have been affected and examine the  rollout of covid recovery funds  meps are expected to call for more  action to combat cyber violence against  women and lgbtiq people proposals  include harmonized criminal sanctions  across the eu for gender-based cyber  violence like cyber stalking and  harassment and the recording of images  of sexual assault  parliament is set to vote on making 2022  the european year of youth  young people have been hit hard by the  pandemic and meps want to hear what they  have to say getting them more involved  in policy making
 

